WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:06.060
Since its inception with 2013's Man of Steel,
the DC Extended Universe encountered obstacle

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:11.420
after obstacle, with poor reviews, mixed reaction
from fans, and disappointing box office receipts.

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:16.110
But there is one potential bright spot on
the horizon: The upcoming Flash solo film,

00:00:16.110 --> 00:00:19.200
which could act as a soft reboot of the entire
universe.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:23.060
So cross your fingers, superhero fans, because
here's a look at why the Flash movie could

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:24.580
fix the DCEU.

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:26.580
Flash to the rescue

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:32.099
Under the guiding hand of director Zack Snyder,
the DCEU was positioned as the dark and gritty

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:34.580
alternative to the bright and fun Marvel movies.

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:38.860
But since being an alternative to fun is a
recipe for failure, the folks at Warner Brothers

00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:43.140
have since changed direction, demoting Snyder
and promoting Walter Hamada to head of the

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:46.680
comic book division in 2018 as an attempt
to lighten things up.

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:51.480
And with the possible exception of Wonder
Woman, no DC hero so far has been as bright

00:00:51.489 --> 00:00:56.840
and upbeat as Ezra Miller's Flash, who added
some much needed levity to 2017's Justice

00:00:56.840 --> 00:00:57.340
League.

00:00:57.340 --> 00:01:01.920
If the DCEU is going to right the ship, the
Flash's brand of spunky fun may be exactly

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:04.460
what Warner Brothers and fans have been hoping
for.

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:05.980
Flashpoint

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:11.600
Though Warner Brothers has reportedly decided
not to name the upcoming Flash film "Flashpoint"

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:15.170
as originally planned, it's still expected
that the movie will draw heavily from the

00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:18.360
popular 2011 Flashpoint comic book storyline.

00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:22.400
That's important, because the plot involves
Barry Allen realizing he's trapped in the

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:27.030
wrong timeline and teaming up with his fellow
heroes to fix time and restore reality to

00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:27.820
its true form.

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:32.290
And that means that Warner Brothers would
have the perfect excuse to jettison any details

00:01:32.290 --> 00:01:35.560
from their previous DCEU films that fans and
critics didn't like.

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:40.860
Things like Pa Kent's weird me-first lessons
on selfishness and amorality, Superman killing

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:45.540
Zod, and the whole Martha scene can be erased
quicker and more successfully than Henry Cavill's

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:46.100
mustache.

00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:50.320
Flashpoint gives Warner brothers a chance
to totally rewrite the history of the DCEU

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:54.320
in order to create a better future for its
characters and its fans.

00:01:55.180 --> 00:01:56.420
The Arrowverse

00:01:57.060 --> 00:02:01.759
If the plot of Flashpoint sounds familiar,
it might be because the CW's Flash TV series

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:04.280
adapted the comic for its third season storyline.

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:08.200
And that suggests another opportunity for
the Flash movie: the multiverse.

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:12.080
In the TV show, of course, Flash and his pals
have discovered that there are lots of alternate

00:02:12.260 --> 00:02:16.980
universes and timelines comprising a multiverse,
which already includes versions of Superman

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:18.580
and Supergirl, among others.

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:22.910
It would be easy and awesome for the film
version of Barry Allen to cross over and meet

00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:25.160
the characters from the CW's Arrowverse.

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:29.960
Considering Flash has consistently been one
of the CW's most popular shows, it's the kind

00:02:29.970 --> 00:02:34.480
of fan service that could bring a whole built-in
audience to the theaters and even give Warner

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:39.120
Brothers a rare leg up on Marvel, which has
struggled to connect its TV shows to its movies.

00:02:39.820 --> 00:02:40.900
Elseworlds

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:46.400
Another benefit to introducing the concept
of the multiverse to the DCEU is that it helps

00:02:46.410 --> 00:02:50.970
explain not just all the previous versions
of DC super-people that have appeared on film,

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:54.160
but all the future out-of-continuity movies
Warner Brothers is planning.

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:57.750
For instance, it's been announced that the
upcoming Joker standalone movie is already

00:02:57.750 --> 00:02:59.940
set to appear in another timeline.

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:03.940
That could be confusing for fans who just
saw a new version of Joker in Suicide Squad,

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:09.590
but if Flash introduces the DCEU to Elseworlds
the name given to alternative universe DC

00:03:09.590 --> 00:03:11.960
superhero stories everything will still make
sense.

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:16.330
And it would also allow Warner Brothers to
recast its big roles with more ease.

00:03:16.330 --> 00:03:20.290
With Ben Affleck constantly rumored to be
leaving as Batman, having some random new

00:03:20.290 --> 00:03:22.180
dude put on the cowl could be jarring.

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:27.480
But if it turns out Affleck is just a wrong
version of Batman from some Elseworlds timeline,

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:29.980
accepting a new star in the role could be
a lot easier.

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:32.500
A tradition of successful reboots

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:37.580
Fans who object to the idea of rebooting the
DCEU through a Flashpoint event this early

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:41.700
on would do well to remember that this wouldn't
be the first time a superhero franchise has

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:44.590
been rebooted and often with great success.

00:03:44.590 --> 00:03:49.560
The X-Men series repeatedly alters its continuity
within the ongoing story, the Batman franchise

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:55.010
was revitalized by Christopher Nolan's trilogy,
and even more recently Spider-Man was reinvigorated

00:03:55.010 --> 00:03:57.380
by Marvel's Tom Holland-led take on the character.

00:03:57.480 --> 00:04:02.120
And just like how Holland's version of Spider-Man
found solo success after breaking out of Captain

00:04:02.120 --> 00:04:06.680
America: Civil War, Ezra Miller's Flash could
do the same following his well-received appearance

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:11.510
in Justice League, all while resetting the
elements of the DCEU that don't work in the

00:04:11.510 --> 00:04:12.100
process.

00:04:12.260 --> 00:04:14.500
Sure, it would be pretty fast for a reboot.

00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:16.460
But after all… nobody is faster than the
Flash.

00:04:16.660 --> 00:04:17.960
Godspeed, Barry Allen!

00:04:18.520 --> 00:04:19.520
Thanks for watching!

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:21.780
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:23.720
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

